# UI and Styling

- Use Shadcn UI for consistent, accessible components
- Use Radix primitives when building custom accessible controls
- Compose small pieces rather than one mega-component
- Style with Tailwind CSS (utility-first)
- Mobile-first responsive layouts
- Dark mode via CSS variables and Tailwind `dark:`
- Meet WCAG contrast for text and interactive states
- Consistent spacing scale; theme colors and spacing as CSS variables

```tsx
<button
	type="button"
	className="rounded-md bg-primary px-4 py-2 text-primary-foreground"
>
	Save
</button>
```
